INT. MAINTENANCE CRAWLSPACE ABOVE CUBICLE FARM - DAY

Ductwork. Dust. A folding chair wedged between pipes. A thermos. A lunch bag labeled "DO NOT TOUCH."

RENATA KOWALCZYK, 40s, lanyard, cardigan, eats a sandwich. Content. A small desk fan hums.

Through the vent grate below: the office. Fluorescent hum. Keyboards.

INTERCOM (V.O.)
Good afternoon, team. A reminder that the quarterly synergy audit begins at three.

Renata chews. Nods. Pours tea.

INTERCOM (V.O.) (CONT'D)
Auditors will be reviewing all workstations. Including unoccupied ones.

She stops chewing.

INTERCOM (V.O.) (CONT'D)
Employee Kowalczyk's desk has been unoccupied for eleven months. Please report to Facilities.

Renata sets down the sandwich. Looks through the grate. Her empty cubicle. A dead plant. Her nameplate.

A flashlight beam sweeps the crawlspace behind her.

RENATA
(whispering)
Oh, no.
